  "caveats": [
    "Industrial sort recovery is not official BC log grade. The bucker is dimension-only; defect, sweep, knot, rot, and product quality are absent.",
    "TIPSY industrial-log curves are model output, not field measurements.",
    "Multiple PSP plots can share one managed AU curve; per-plot RMSE is therefore not an independent model-error estimate.",
    "Bucked volume is expanded with FAIB PHF_TREE to m3/ha and compared with the TIPSY industrial total at the same AU/age. Plot sums are m3/ha sums, not absolute volume.",
    "The canonical managed_au_industrial_sorts.csv in tsa24_grade_curves is empty because the refreshed BTC run did not request the industrial-logs indicator bank; this validation records the separately compiled table it used and fails closed when no table is available."
  ],
